# Reference for what this project reads. Everything here is NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which
# means it is inlined at BUILD time, so a change needs a rebuild and redeploy.
#
# Note the real production values live in the COMMITTED `.env`, not in a
# gitignored `.env.local`. Nothing this project reads is a secret, and a
# build-time variable that exists only on one machine is a variable the
# deployed site does not have.

# Canonical site origin, used by robots.ts and sitemap.ts. Defaults to
# https://mythcorp.org when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mythcorp.org

# Chrome origin trial tokens, rendered as <meta http-equiv="origin-trial"> in
# src/app/layout.tsx. Leave empty and nothing is rendered.
#
# What we want it for: the html-in-canvas trial, which turns on
# ctx.drawElementImage and canvas.requestPaint. Without it, Asciify,
# DecryptReveal, RetroDither and Glitch in src/app/components/canvasui/ are
# inert for anyone who has not enabled chrome://flags/#canvas-draw-element.
#
# Register at https://developer.chrome.com/origintrials, trial "html-in-canvas"
# (feature name HTMLInCanvas). One token per origin, so mythcorp.org,
# i.mythcorp.org and the *.workers.dev preview host each need one unless you
# tick "match all subdomains" at registration. List them comma separated.
#
# Tokens expire. This trial's current window ends 2026-10-20 (Chrome 148 to
# 154). An expired token fails silently, so if those effects go quiet, look
# here first.
#
# A live token for https://mythcorp.org (with subdomain matching, so
# i.mythcorp.org is covered) is already set in `.env`. Still unregistered, each
# needing its own token: the *.workers.dev preview host, and
# http://localhost:3000 if you want to exercise these components on a dev
# server rather than only in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN=
